  "step_3": "The decision reason relies on calculating an aspiration level from the mean of all outcomes and then favoring the lottery with the higher probability of exceeding this level. The relevant information includes the set of possible outcomes, their comparison to a computed reference point (≈ -2333.33), and the probabilities of positive deviations. However, the individual does not mention or imply any calculation of an average outcome, nor do they refer to a threshold or reference point against which outcomes are evaluated. Instead, their reasoning centers on the certainty of A versus the risk of B, particularly the 80% chance of a large loss and 20% chance of zero in B. The justification is consistent with a certainty effect or risk aversion, not with evaluating outcomes relative to an aspiration level. There is no alignment between the information considered by the individual and that required by the decision reason. Similarly, the justification (certainty as advantage, no risks) does not match the rule of the decision reason (prefer higher probability of positive differences). Therefore, it is highly unlikely that the individual used this decision reason.",
