  "step_1": "The decision reason is based on an aspiration level defined as the mean of all outcomes across both lotteries, ignoring probabilities. The outcomes in the decision problem are: -4000, 0 (from Lottery B), and -3000, 0 (from Lottery A). Ignoring probabilities, the unique outcomes are -4000, -3000, and 0. The mean (aspiration level) is (-4000 + (-3000) + 0) / 3 = -7000 / 3 ≈ -2333.33 Euros. The reason evaluates each lottery based on the probability that its outcomes exceed this aspiration level (i.e., yield a positive difference). For Lottery A: -3000 < -2333.33 (difference negative), 0 > -2333.33 (positive difference); this occurs with 75% probability. For Lottery B: -4000 < -2333.33 (negative), 0 > -2333.33 (positive); this occurs with 80% probability. Thus, Lottery B has a higher probability (80% vs 75%) of yielding a positive difference from the aspiration level and would be preferred by this reason. The decision reason is applicable to the problem.",
