  "step_3": "The decision reason relies on computing an aspiration level (-3000) and comparing outcomes to it, then favoring the lottery with a higher probability of positive deviations. Both lotteries have 75% chance of outcomes above -3000, so the reason does not favor one over the other. The individual, however, based their choice on minimizing the potential loss, specifically focusing on the worst loss in each lottery (-6000 in A vs. -4000 in B). This suggests a focus on loss aversion or minimax regret, not on deviations from an aspiration level. The information considered by the individual (size of losses) differs from that required by the reason (deviations from -3000). The justification (minimize loss if loss occurs) does not align with the reason’s rule (maximize chance of positive difference from aspiration). There is no indication that the individual computed an average of all outcomes or evaluated deviations from it. Therefore, the decision reason was not used.",
